minttweaks (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Maintenance module: measured disk usage, a preview of what apt-get
    autoremove would delete, cleanup tasks, and kernel removal that never
    touches the running or the newest kernel.
  * Services module: systemd unit list with start/stop/enable/disable, the
    per-unit journal, and a boot analysis.
  * Samba module: installation, share and account management, an smb.conf
    editor validated with testparm, backups, plus ufw and smbstatus helpers.
  * Privileged writes go through a narrow polkit helper (mtk-root).
  * French interface translation.

 -- Gabriel Chapdelaine <gabriel@localhost>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:07:32 -0400
